{
 "_about": [
  "Skwoop's spoken action acknowledgements. Each (kind, mood) bucket has its own lines, worded for that mood.",
  "Moods are the approved Skwoop mood loops (skwoop-2d/loops) that can speak: idle (= the tone classifier's neutral), happy, sad, sleep, thinking, alert.",
  "A bucket is a list of lines, or {\"tags\": [...], \"takes\": n, \"lines\": [...]}. 'tags' default to the top-level ones for that mood.",
  "Each line is recorded 'takes' times (default: top-level takes), each take with a different tag from the bucket, chosen by the line's text so edits don't reshuffle other lines.",
  "Tags are Eleven v4 audio tags, sent in front of the line on ElevenLabs renders only. Sleep tags are cute-tired ([yawns] is a reaction tag like the documented [laughs]/[sighs]); no hum openers (Mm, Mmhm, Ooh) and no soft/hushed/breathy tags, which made the sleepy lines sound like moaning.",
  "'default' is the kind's mood when the request gives none and the pod has no fresh mood this kind has a bucket for.",
  "Rendered once with ElevenLabs (render_acks.py, deleted Oct 6 2026; see git history before the an earlier revision round)."
 ],
 "takes": 3,
 "tags": {
  "happy": [
   "[cheerfully]",
   "[brightly]",
   "[warmly, with a smile]"
  ],
  "idle": [
   "[warmly]",
